#~ crosses the boundary
# A driver may not return a shape.
#
# The rule this file exists for cost a real bug: `vertex_at` declared as
# returning a three-i32 shape compiled, linked, ran — and lost two of
# the three fields. A 12-byte aggregate returns through a hidden pointer
# on SysV, and the generated code returned it by value.
#
# It failed with `x` still correct, which is the worst possible failure:
# a careless test passes. Nothing about it was catchable at run time,
# and it was written two screens below a comment saying not to do it.
#
# So the compiler enforces it. Integers and handles cross; anything with
# a layout does not.

shape Vertex
  x i32
  y i32
  z i32

driver fn vertex_at(index i32) Vertex

test "t"
  throw "x" unless vertex_at(index: 0).x == 0
